# Who reviews what. GitHub applies the LAST pattern that matches a path, so the
# maintainer-only paths come last: a broader rule added above can never take them away.

# Everything, by default.
*                                               @artemkozak

# Service modules (every module change is reviewed). A service's maintainer is added
# beside the project maintainer on that service's folder, one line each, BELOW the next line, for example:
#   /packages/services/src/services/<id>/       @artemkozak @<maintainer>
/packages/services/src/services/                @artemkozak

# Project maintainer only: the core, the protocol, what a module may do, and the security-relevant parts of
# the extension, its build and its release.
